  "description": "After a short stress task (serial subtraction), each participant is randomly assigned to one of four settings (mountainous, terraced or flatland peony garden, or an indoor office) and views its six 360° scenes for one minute each, then rates stress again and completes the Perceived Restorativeness Scale. Rebuilt from Zhao, Ma, Zhang, Hu & Zhang (2026), Frontiers in Psychology 17: 1935645, with the paper's 24 panoramic photographs (Figure 2, CC BY 4.0).",
